  "texts": {
    "preamble": "State Of Rajasthan vs Rambilash on 20 February, 2018 High Court Of Judicature For Rajasthan Bench At Jaipur S.B. Criminal Leave To Appeal No. 264 / 2015 State Of Rajasthan ----Appellant Versus Rambilash ----Respondent",
    "facts": "The accused respondent was tried for offence under Section 7/16 of Food Adulteration Act. On 11.10.2000 at 9:00 AM, Food Inspector was on adulteration prevention drive. On suspicion, from the shop of accused respondent, out of 50 Kg Khoa, 750 gm of Khoa was purchased by making payment of Rs.45/-. Thereafter, three different sample bottles were prepared of the above said Khoa, and in each bottle twenty drops of Formalin were also mixed and thereafter they were sealed. After following due procedure, samples were sent to the Public Analyst. After report was received, samples were declared adulterated by the State Public Analyst. The argument was raised before the trial court that right of the accused to get the second sample tested from Central Food Laboratory has been breached in the present case.",
